# One appetite rising
# Each body has two appetites, called O and P. They are not visible in themselves - what
# you see is the light that follows them: the brighter that light, the hungrier the body.
# This file describes one single appetite, from switch-on onwards. The times below are
# exact (the artwork counts them itself), unlike the movement times elsewhere, which are
# estimates. They assume an appetite starting from empty; the bodies are set up starting
# part-filled, so in practice each one reaches these points a little sooner.

0 The appetite starts at a value between 0 and 100, set in advance for each body. They are deliberately different, so the five bodies do not all wake up at the same moment.
30 It grows by one point every 2.4 seconds, always at that speed. Below about 12 points the body counts as satisfied for this appetite, so it takes half a minute to leave that state.
150 It keeps growing at the same steady rate. At 75 points the body counts as frustrated for this appetite - three minutes from empty.
60 It goes on growing for one more minute and then reaches 100 and stops. Four minutes from empty to full.
0 Nothing in the artwork ever lowers an appetite again: no encounter, no exchange, no passage of time brings it back down. Only a person, from the control page, can reset it.
0 So every appetite you watch only ever climbs, and after four minutes every appetite in the room is simply full and stays full for the rest of the evening.
